since I started this with my idea that certain classes should get "free
identifys" on specific types of objects (i.e. Archaeologists get with
gems), let me clarify my standpoint regarding Rick Lindsley's posting

I do not feel that classes should get an identify as per the spell
or scroll, only priests should intrinsicly know if an item is blessed
or cursed. What I would like to se, for example, is:

Knights know armor so when they find a pair of padded gloves they would know
what padded gloves were (gauntlets of power, fumbling, leather gloves, or
whatever) but not know whether it is blessed or cursed or + or -
Archaeologist do not know if gems are blessed or cursed, only what kind
they are. So a Barbarian, for example, would know that the runed dagger he
just picked up was an elven dagger but not if its safe

The same argument applies to the other classes in my example.
